Skip derivations that only exist on a remote store instead of spamming
DerivationReadError.

With `--store ssh-ng://... --eval-store auto` nix keeps .drv files on the
remote store, so the local openFile in getDerivation fails with ENOENT for
every derivation nix reports. lookupDerivation never marked those as
cached, so each build event retried the read and emitted another

  nix-output-monitor error: DerivationReadError ...: openFile: does not exist

Treat isDoesNotExistError as "remote drv, no local graph": mark the node
cached with empty inputs (a leaf in the forest) and emit no error. Genuine
read errors (permissions, IO) still surface. Upstream issue:
maralorn/nix-output-monitor#175.

